    "All new external work shall be in materials to match the existing building or carried out in materials as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The glazing serving the ground floor window and door in the side elevation of the development indicated on drawing No SE/2PC/02 shall be fixed shut 1.7m above floor level and in obscured glass with an equivalent obscuration as level 3 on the Pilkington Obscuration Range. The glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties.\r"
